From: alice@example.com
To: bob@example.org
Subject: Alternative bodies and attachments
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary=outer

--outer
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=notes.txt

This attachment must not become the message body.
--outer
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary=inner

--inner
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64

UGxhaW4gYWx0ZXJuYXRpdmUu
--inner
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

<p>HTML alternative.</p>
--inner--
--outer
Content-Type: message/rfc822
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=forwarded.eml

From: other@example.net
Subject: Attached message
Content-Type: text/plain

Attached message body must not replace the outer body.
--outer--
